# Refrain
#
# Ambient by process, not by tune. Db major, 3/4, 63 bpm.
#
#   harmony  an 8-bar loop that never cadences — Gbmaj7 | Db/F | Ebm9 |
#            Ab7sus4 — with Cbmaj7#11 (the borrowed flat seventh)
#            standing in for Ebm9 a few times: the one surprise.
#   refrain  four notes from the Db pentatonic (Db Eb F Ab Bb), every one
#            consonant over every chord, the borrowed one included. Its
#            loop is 7 bars against the harmony's 8, so each pass lands a
#            bar later: the same notes, recoloured by a different chord
#            every time, realigning only after 56 bars.
#   second   a three-note refrain, higher, on a 9-bar loop, for the middle.
#
# Mix (from measuring the last piece): each refrain is a single saw — no
# detuned pair beating against itself — that blooms open instead of
# pinging; it sits off-centre and level with the pads, inside its own
# ping-pong echoes, not dry on top of them. Pads drier and brighter. No
# chorus, no wow, no vibrato, no bus compressor. About 7.5 dB between the
# quiet ends and the middle.
#
# 63 bpm, 3 beats a bar; bar n starts at beat 3*(n-1). 144 bars.

bpm 63
gate 0.97
tail 14

# ------------------------------------------------------------- refrain

track refrain vel=0.55 patch=init gain=0.7 pan=-0.25 echo_send=0.45 reverb_send=0.2
R:45
(R:1 Ab4:1 F5:5 Eb5:2 Db5:5 R:7)x16
automate refrain.attack
0.25
automate refrain.decay
2
automate refrain.sustain
0.85
automate refrain.release
2.5
automate refrain.osc3_wave
3
automate refrain.osc3_pitch
12
automate refrain.osc3_level
0 R:150 0.14:60@smooth R:120 0:60@smooth
automate refrain.hpf
200
automate refrain.resonance
0.15
automate refrain.key_track
0.6
automate refrain.filter_env
0.5
automate refrain.filter_attack
0.6
automate refrain.filter_decay
3
automate refrain.filter_sustain
0.6
automate refrain.filter_release
2
automate refrain.cutoff
650 R:45 1300:100@smooth 1900:130@smooth R:40 900:100@smooth

